R | 76 Wood Products | 7,252 Corporate | 868 Total | 9,517","context":"Our employees by business segment were as follows:","section":"In our Management’s Discussion and Analysis of Financial Condition and Results of Operations (MD&A) section you will find discussion of our overall performance results for our business segments, which are as follows:","block":116,"table":" | \nSEGMENT | NUMBER OF EMPLOYEES\nTimberlands | 1,321\nReal Estate & ENR | 76\nWood Products | 7,252\nCorporate | 868\nTotal | 9,517","attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001193125-26-051422","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-13","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0000106535","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/106535/000119312526051422/wy-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/abf4024ff6d891854e12bc51d2ea034adf6433d66e8a2a326a5030f52672ed2e.bin","sha256":"abf4024ff6d891854e12bc51d2ea034adf6433d66e8a2a326a5030f52672ed2e"}},{"id":"2f2dc34cf8ac1c9df2f49215b0e5a04d1ff89bbb9d36955297bdb5ab361890bb","quote":"We are committed to continual improvement and do so through annual prevention-based goals, our internal Safety Council, external benchmarking, implementation of new technology, replicating key learnings and enhancing our safety system and process. Our efforts have resulted in a significant and sustained reduction in the number and severity of recordable injuries over time. This includes a drop in our Recordable Incident Rate, which is the number of Occupational Safety and Health Administration-defined recordable injuries and illnesses that occur per 100 workers working in one year, from 3.85 in 2000 to 2.17 in 2025.","context":"building and verifying safety skills.","section":"In our Management’s Discussion and Analysis of Financial Condition and Results of Operations (MD&A) section you will find discussion of our overall performance results for our business segments, which are as follows:","block":131,"table":null,"